    "2) Define Convolutional Neural Networks (CNNs) and discuss their role in image processing.Describe the key advantages of using CNNs over traditional neural  networks for image-related tasks. \n",
    "\n",
    "Ans:-\n",
    "A Convolutional Neural Network (CNN) is a special type of deep learning \n",
    "model designed mainly for image processing and computer vision tasks. \n",
    "It automatically learns to detect important features from images such as edges, \n",
    "textures, shapes, and objects, without needing manual feature extraction. \n",
    "CNNs work by passing the image through multiple layers like convolution layers, \n",
    "pooling layers, and fully connected layers, where each layer learns different \n",
    "features of the image. \n",
    "\n",
    "Role of CNNs in Image Processing: \n",
    "1. Feature Extraction: \n",
    "CNNs automatically extract important visual features (like edges, corners, and \n",
    "colors) from raw image data. \n",
    "\n",
    "2. Pattern Recognition: \n",
    "They identify complex patterns such as faces, animals, or objects within the \n",
    "image. \n",
    "\n",
    "3. Image Classification: \n",
    "CNNs are widely used to classify images into categories (e.g., dog vs. cat). \n",
    "\n",
    "4. Object Detection and Segmentation: \n",
    "They help locate and label multiple objects in an image accurately. \n",
    "\n",
    "5. Image Enhancement and Restoration: \n",
    "CNNs are also used for tasks like denoising, super-resolution, and removing blur. \n",
    "\n",
    "Main Advantages of CNNs: \n",
    "1. Automatic feature learning – no need for manual feature extraction. \n",
    "2. Translation invariance – can recognize objects regardless of their position. \n",
    "3. Parameter efficiency – fewer weights to train compared to fully connected \n",
    "networks. \n",
    "4. High accuracy – performs exceptionally well on image recognition, \n",
    "classification, and detection tasks."
   ]
  },
